            <ArticleTitle>4-Azetidinyl-1-heteroatom linked cyclohexane antagonists of CCR2: patent evaluation.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1275-80</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1517/13543776.2011.584872</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>This application discloses a series of di- and tri-substituted cyclohexanes as CCR2 receptor antagonists which are stated to be useful in treating inflammation and autoimmune diseases, such as type 2 diabetes and asthma. Although receptor binding of the compounds to CCR2 is demonstrated, there are no data to support the idea that these molecules are functional antagonists.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
